/-!
# Ambient cubic geometry for the long frame

The long cubic is proved fixed-free on the whole binary Leech module.
`LocalData` transports common centralizers by the actual Conway conjugator
and reduces the two placement inputs to relative fixed-free cubic fusion
and the marked root cubic's fixed-vector and centralizer calculations.
Those model premises remain explicit; this module does not yet assert
unconditional ambient placement or centralizer saturation.

Source: Aschbacher, *Sporadic Groups* (1994), 49.1–49.2, p.280,
and the proof of 49.5, pp.283–284.
-/
